        "date": "2026-11-21T08:46:47Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(2d): close Zigzag pockets with wall and island rings\n\nA Zigzag pocket (and Auto, which resolves to Zigzag) cut only rows. The\nrows touch a side wall or an island only at their ends, so a cusp stood\nbetween each two ends over the full depth (0.17 mm on a straight wall,\n0.75 mm on a rounded corner, 6 mm tall in the report). Verify passed it.\n\nEach Zigzag pocket now uses the rest pocket's plan: rows 0.01 mm inside\nthe cutter-center area, then one closed ring on each boundary loop.\nThe row points stand on the 1 um lattice. Off-lattice starts made two\nlevels' helix entries at one point read as crossing chords.\n\nTests: pocket_wall_finish (new); setup_align and corner_blend laws that\nassumed rows only are corrected. The pocket_zigzag_plate_with_island\ngoldens and the two first-part sample programs are regenerated.\n\nFixes #3021\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
